.TH SSH 1 "" "Helios" "User commands"
.SH NAME
ssh \- log into another machine using SSH
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ssh
.RB [ \-t | \-T ]
.RB [ \-p " port" ]
.RB [ \-l " user" ]
.RB [ \-i " private-key" ]
.RB [ \-K " hosts-file" ]
.RI [ user @] host
.RI [ command " ..."]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The native Helios client connects to an SSH server and opens a remote shell
or executes a command. The supplied provider performs SSH negotiation and
cryptography in a worker inside the Linux I/O server. The host must have
SSH support enabled; the client never falls back to an unencrypted login.
.PP
Without a command, a terminal is requested when standard input is a terminal.
Its TERM, rows and columns are sent to the server. Window changes are forwarded
on SIGWINCH. Input is put in raw mode and restored when the client exits;
Ctrl-C is passed to the remote terminal. Nonterminal input supports file
redirection and EOF. Remote stdout and stderr are merged by this provider.
.PP
For an interactive xterm, the client queries its character encoding, enables
UTF-8 for the remote session and restores the previous encoding on exit.
Terminals without the encoding query remain unchanged. Redirected output is
not modified with terminal control sequences.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-t
Request a remote terminal, including for a command or redirected input.
.TP
.B \-T
Do not request a remote terminal.
.TP
.BI \-p " port"
Connect to this port instead of 22.
.TP
.BI \-l " user"
Remote account name. user@host takes precedence. The default is USER or LOGNAME.
.TP
.BI \-i " private-key"
Read the private key from a Helios file, at most 8192 bytes. The client prompts
for its passphrase; press Return for an unencrypted key. If key authentication
fails and the server offers passwords, the client can try a password.
.TP
.BI \-K " hosts-file"
Use this host-key file instead of $HOME/.ssh/hosts.
.SH HOST KEYS AND AUTHENTICATION
The client shows an unknown host's key type and SHA-256 fingerprint and asks
whether to remember it. Answer yes to append the entry. A changed key is
rejected. This client's hosts file is plain text with hostname, port, key type
and fingerprint on each line; it is separate from OpenSSH's known_hosts format.
.PP
Password prompts disable terminal echo. Public-key and password authentication
are supported; keyboard-interactive authentication, agent forwarding, SFTP,
port forwarding, X11 forwarding and OpenSSH configuration files are not
implemented in this version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The remote command's exit status, or 255 for a connection, authentication or
local error. Usage errors return 2.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ssh alice@server
ssh -p 2222 -i /helios/users/alice/.ssh/id_ed25519 alice@server
ssh alice@server uname -a
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
hu_ssh(3), hu_terminal(3), helios-unix(7)
